memory mapping can be shared or private


Memory mapping can be shared or private

Shared mapping:
multiple processes can share a mapping(
  like in pipes, can fork a process, and the process can have the same mapping)(the data is also
  shared, if you change one, this part of the data is also changed in the parent process.

multiple processes can map the same file.


shared mapping

  that part of the memory is mapped to the same page.
  if you change the contents of one process
  it changes in the other one.

private
  copy on write
  when we fork, the memory mapping points to the same page, but if the child process starts writing
  to the memory mapping, the data in the memory is copied over and then the memory mappping points
  to a different page/frame

  the address it points to in the vram is still the same, but it is different in the physical
  memory.

4 Possibilties:
  Private file mapping:
    file is mapped to a memroy/process as  a private mapping
      Changes not written to file or shared with other processes.

    so when we fork, the memory mapping can be accessed, when we write to it,
      it will be like anonymous, won't write to the file.
  Shared file mapping:
    changes propogate to the real file eventually.

    other processes mapping same file.

  Private anonymous mapping:
    more memory is allocated ot the calling process
      fork() copies memory but each process has private

  Shared anonymous
    memory is shared, changes propogate to other process
